-- The iteration module under its former name, for the committed bootstrap.
--
-- `bootstrap/`'s compiler gives every module with the Prelude this module as
-- the qualifier `Iterator`, and the compiler's own source, which that compiler
-- builds, writes `Iterator.any`. So this module must exist and re-export what
-- `src/` calls. Everything else uses `Iter`.
export (any, all, count, find)

import Prelude ()
import Iter (any, all, count, find)
